* [`ag.cohen_macaulay_type`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Background/Algebraic-geometry/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_ag___cohen_macaulay_type_FLQQ_--statement) — Cohen-Macaulay type. Difficulty: hard, theory. *Blocked by:* canonical modules of orders (the definition; that the trace dual Rᵗ is one; that any two are locally isomorphic, so that the minimal number of generators of the localisations does not depend on the choice). Proved for every order in an étale ℚ-algebra (round AM): Rᵗ is a fractional ideal, the type is attained at a maximal ideal and is at least 1, type 1 iff Rᵗ is invertible iff every I with (I : I) = R is invertible, and (Rᵗ : (Rᵗ : I)) = I. Note: Done: Round AM (AM4\_etale\_orders, optional knowl), kept partial; the first half of the blocker is closed. Round AF's part (i), 'orders in etale Q-algebras that are not fields', is now proved for every order R in an etale Q-algebra K (with K nontrivial where a maximal ideal is needed): the trace form of K is nondegenerate (traceForm\_nondegenerate\_of\_etale, from traceForm\_nondegenerate\_of\_isReduced), so R\^t = \{a : Tr(aR) in Z\} is a finitely generated R-module (Subalgebra.fg\_traceDual\_of\_isLattice) containing R (Tr(R) in Z, trace\_mem\_range\_of\_isLattice) and a fractional ideal (Subalgebra.traceDualFractionalIdeal); the type, max over maximal ideals l of dim\_\{R/l\} R\^t/lR\^t, is a maximum attained at some l and at least 1 (cohenMacaulayTypeAt\_le\_cohenMacaulayType\_of\_isLattice, exists\_cohenMacaulayTypeAt\_eq\_cohenMacaulayType\_of\_isLattice, one\_le\_cohenMacaulayType\_of\_isLattice); it is 1 iff R\^t is invertible (cohenMacaulayType\_eq\_one\_iff\_isUnit\_traceDualFractionalIdeal); and the order is Gorenstein iff every fractional ideal I (with a non-zero-divisor) with (I : I) = R is invertible (isGorenstein\_iff\_forall\_isUnit\_of\_isLattice), the corrected last sentence, through the duality I -\> I\^t with I\^tt = I, (I : I) = (I I\^t)\^t and (R\^t : R\^t) = R. These supersede the number-field-only results of CohenMacaulayType.lean. Also proved: (R\^t : (R\^t : I)) = I for every fractional ideal I (traceDual\_div\_traceDual\_div), the Herzog-Kunz characterisation of a canonical ideal of a one-dimensional Cohen-Macaulay ring, so R\^t is canonical in that ideal-theoretic sense. Not formalised: canonical modules. No tree defines them; taking the ideal-theoretic property as the definition would be a model of the knowl's notion (the 11-06 ruling) until its equivalence with the standard one (a maximal Cohen-Macaulay module of type 1 and finite injective dimension, locally) is proved; and 'the Cohen-Macaulay type is the minimal number of generators of a canonical module' (read locally, as recorded) needs the count to be independent of the canonical module chosen: two canonical modules are locally isomorphic (differ by an invertible ideal), not proved. Text corrections recorded before (local number of generators; '(I:I)' -\> '(I:I) = R') stand. Blocked by: canonical modules of orders (definition; R\^t is one; any two are locally isomorphic, so the local number of generators does not depend on the choice). Difficulty: hard. No category field (LeanBridge decls). Knock-on, for the lead: av.fq.bass\_zfv's blocker part 'Gorenstein orders in etale Q-algebras that are not fields (ag.cohen\_macaulay\_type)' is now proved (Gorenstein iff R\^t invertible iff proper fractional ideals invertible, every etale order); the hypothesis hpos (types at least 1) of Subalgebra.isBass\_iff\_maxCohenMacaulayType\_eq\_one now holds for the overorders of an order in a nontrivial etale Q-algebra (they are lattices; one\_le\_cohenMacaulayType\_of\_isLattice), not stated as a lemma here; finiteness of the overorders stays open. Review (AM4\_etale\_orders, 2026-11-17, review/AM4\_etale\_orders.md): partial, confirmed. The etale half of round AF's blocker is closed as recorded (R\^t finitely generated through the nondegenerate trace form, a fractional ideal containing R; the type bounds the local types, is attained and is at least 1 for K nonzero; type 1 iff R\^t invertible iff every I with (I : I) = R is invertible; (R\^t : (R\^t : I)) = I). Sentence 1 (canonical modules) and the claim 'R\^t is a canonical module' stay unformalised; the step from the local minimal number of generators to dim R\^t/lR\^t is a small bridge (Mathlib's IsLocalRing.spanFinrank\_eq\_finrank\_quotient after localising at l). Blocked by: canonical modules of orders (the definition; that R\^t is one; that any two are locally isomorphic, so that the minimal number of generators of the localisations does not depend on the choice). New pure typo recorded: 'The \*\*Cohen-Macaulay\*\* type of an order \$R\$,' -\> 'The \*\*Cohen-Macaulay type\*\* of an order \$R\$'. Knock-ons (exact lines in the review): av.fq.bass\_zfv drops 'Gorenstein orders in etale Q-algebras that are not fields (ag.cohen\_macaulay\_type)' from its blocker; av.fq.max\_cohen\_macaulay\_type's blocker narrows ag.cohen\_macaulay\_type to its canonical modules.
