* [`ag.kodaira_dimension`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Background/Algebraic-geometry/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_ag___kodaira_dimension_FLQQ_--statement) — Kodaira dimension. Difficulty: hard, information. *Blocked by:* a corrected knowl (d ≥ 1, X projective or proper), and finiteness of H⁰(X, K\^\{⊗d\}) for proper X (so that P\_d is defined and ℙ(H⁰) ≅ ℙ\^\{P\_d-1\}). Note: Done: Partial by the sweep of 2026-11-06 (the user's rulings: when in doubt, partial; an unproved fact stated in the knowl makes it partial; a model of the knowl's object is partial): corrected. As written the definition is degenerate: P₀ = h⁰(X, 𝒪\_X) ≥ 1 for nonempty X, so 'P\_d = 0 for all d ∈ ℤ≥0' never holds and the literal sup over d ≥ 0 gives κ(ℙ¹) = 0 instead of -1; for non-proper X, H⁰(X, K\^\{⊗d\}) can be infinite-dimensional (𝔸¹). LeanBridge formalises the corrected definition (sup over d ≥ 1, ⊥ when no K\^\{⊗d\} with d ≥ 1 has a nonzero section), and its comparison lemmas assume Module.Finite k H⁰(X, K\^\{⊗d\}). Difficulty raised from easy to hard: the corrected text still needs this finiteness for proper X, a coherence theorem that the trees have only for curves. Not formalised: “Let \$X\$ be a nonsingular complex algebraic variety ... For each \$d \\in \\mathbb\{Z\}\_\{\\geq 0\}\$ ... The Kodaira dimension \$\\kappa(X)\$ is defined to be \$-1\$ if \$P\_d = 0\$ for all \$d\$”.
