* [`alg.symplectic_isomorphism`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Background/Ring-theory/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_alg___symplectic_isomorphism_FLQQ_--statement) — Symplectic isomorphism. Difficulty: hard, theory. *Blocked by:* the finite étale group-scheme variant that the knowl's text includes: the exterior square of a group scheme (or alternating pairings G ×\_S G → μ\_N of group schemes) and the notion of being (ℤ/Nℤ)² étale locally, in neither tree (Tau Ceti has μ\_N as a group scheme). Note: Done: All but the étale variant is now formalised. 'Or equivalently a nondegenerate alternating pairing': rootsOfUnity.exteriorSquareEquivPairing is a bijection between isomorphisms α : ⋀²M ≃ μ\_N and nondegenerate alternating pairings M × M → μ\_N (α ↦ (x, y) ↦ α(x ∧ y)), for M free of rank 2 over ℤ/N and μ\_N in a separably (e.g. algebraically) closed field of characteristic prime to N; its core is LinearMap.injective\_iff\_separatingLeft (any commutative ring, through the trivialisation Module.Basis.exteriorSquareEquiv : ⋀²M ≃ R, x ∧ y ↦ det(x, y)) and bijective\_iff\_nondegenerate (\|μ\_N\| = N). Examples: E\[N\] with Tau Ceti's Weil pairing (weilPairingExteriorEquiv, S ∧ T ↦ e\_N(S, T), for W over F and K a separably closed extension); ℤ/N × μ\_N with the determinant pairing (detSymplecticEquiv, with toMul\_detPairing giving the knowl's δ\^a/γ\^b, nondegenerate\_detPairing, and the basis (1, 0), (0, ζ)). Galois-module variant: LinearEquiv.IsGaloisSymplectic (equivariant and symplectic; -1 is an instance, isGaloisSymplectic\_neg), with G acting on ⋀²M by Tau Ceti's Representation.exteriorPower ρ 2; both examples are Galois-equivariant (isIntertwiningMap\_weilPairingExteriorEquiv via Tau Ceti's weilPairing\_torsionGaloisAction, for LeanBridge's mod-N representation modGaloisRepresentation; isIntertwiningMap\_detSymplecticEquiv for any action on μ\_N). Still missing: 'or replaced by a finite étale group scheme that is (ℤ/Nℤ)² étale locally', the same definition for a finite étale group scheme G over a base S, étale locally isomorphic to (ℤ/Nℤ)², with α : ⋀²G ≃ μ\_N. Tau Ceti at the pin has commutative group schemes (group objects of Over S), constant group schemes, finite étale schemes over an affine base and μ\_N as a group scheme (TauCeti.RootsOfUnityGroup.groupScheme), but neither tree has the second exterior power of a group scheme (or alternating pairings G ×\_S G → μ\_N of group schemes) nor the notion of being (ℤ/Nℤ)² étale locally; Tau Ceti's main has finite étale group schemes as group objects only (round ZZ). No text error.
