* [`group.min_faithful_linear`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Abstract-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_group___min_faithful_linear_FLQQ_--statement) — Minimal faithful linear representations. Difficulty: hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The lower bound of the Schur-index sentence: m\_k(χ) divides the multiplicity of χ in every character afforded over k (Isaacs, Cor. 10.2), over ℚ (the simple components of ℚ\[G\] as matrix algebras over division algebras of index m, a missing theory) and over ℝ (where the upper bound is missing too). The user's ruling of 2026-11-13: the sentence means exactly m copies are needed. Note: Done: Round AG (AG1); partial, three of the four round-AF blockers closed and the fourth half closed. (i) 'there may be no faithful irreducible representations of G' (AF blocker i): closed. A finite abelian group with a faithful irreducible complex representation is cyclic (isCyclic\_of\_injective\_of\_isIrreducible: the representation is one-dimensional, Mathlib's IsIrreducible.finrank\_eq\_one\_of\_isMulCommutative, so G embeds in C\^x, isCyclic\_of\_injective\_ringHom), so a non-cyclic finite abelian group has irr\_C(G) = -1 (irreducibleDegree\_complex\_eq\_neg\_one\_of\_not\_isCyclic), in particular every Klein four-group, Mathlib's IsKleinFour class, e.g. Multiplicative (ZMod 2 x ZMod 2) (IsKleinFour.irreducibleDegree\_complex\_eq\_neg\_one); faithful representations exist (AF's toHomUnits\_permMatrixHom\_comp\_injective). (ii) 'computing lin\_C(G) requires finding linear combinations of characters that are faithful' (AF blocker ii): closed. G has a faithful matrix representation of degree n over C exactly when some N-combination psi = sum m\_i chi\_i of the rows of Tau Ceti's character table with sum m\_i chi\_i(1) = n is faithful, psi(g) = n only at g = 1 (exists\_injective\_iff\_exists\_nsmul\_sum: forward by Tau Ceti's character\_eq\_sum\_nsmul\_irreducibleCharacter, backward by direct sums of the row representations, FDRep.exists\_character\_eq\_sum\_nsmul, and a basis, FDRep.exists\_representation\_character\_eq; faithfulness by AF's Representation.injective\_iff\_character\_eq\_character\_one), so lin\_C(G) is the least degree of a faithful N-combination (linearDegree\_complex\_eq). (iii) the Galois-orbit sentence for k = R (AF blocker iii): closed. FDRep.realGaloisConjugates (sigma o chi, sigma in Gal(C/R)) = \{chi, conj o chi\} (realGaloisConjugates\_eq); FDRep.realCharacter, their sum, is chi when chi is real valued and chi + conj chi otherwise (realCharacter\_eq\_of\_conj\_comp\_eq, realCharacter\_eq\_add); for irreducible chi it is a real valued character, of a direct sum (exists\_real\_character\_eq\_realCharacter), faithful iff chi is (realCharacter\_faithful\_iff, from the new FDRep.sum\_faithful\_iff for any set s of Aut(C)-conjugates of chi containing chi, s a subset of FDRep.galoisConjugates and hence finite, through FDRep.realGaloisConjugates\_subset\_galoisConjugates; the argument of AF's rationalCharacter\_faithful\_iff, which is the case s = galoisConjugates), and each summand is faithful iff chi is (faithful\_iff\_of\_mem\_realGaloisConjugates); k = Q was AF's (FDRep.rationalCharacter\_faithful\_iff, FDRep.algEquiv\_comp\_faithful\_iff). (iv) the Schur-index sentence (AF blocker iv): half closed. Upper bound, in general over Q: for an irreducible complex representation with character chi and Schur index m = FDRep.schurIndex Q (the LMFDB's least \[E : Q(chi)\]), m times the irreducible rational character psi = sum of the distinct Galois conjugates is the character of a representation over Q (FDRep.exists\_character\_eq\_schurIndex\_mul\_rationalCharacter): restriction of scalars of a realisation over E with \[E : Q(chi)\] = m (FDRep.exists\_character\_eq\_trace, Tau Ceti's LinearMap.trace\_restrictScalars), Tr\_\{E/Q\}(x) = \[E : K\] Tr\_\{K/Q\}(x) for x in K (IntermediateField.trace\_inclusion, by sums of roots of the minimal polynomial), and Tr\_\{Q(chi)/Q\}(chi(g)) = psi(g) (FDRep.sum\_algHom\_characterField\_eq\_rationalCharacter: embeddings of Q(chi) extend to Aut(C), LeanBridge's exists\_algEquiv\_apply\_eq\_of\_countable). The knowl's example completed (AF's 'or at least'): the two-dimensional character chi of Q8 is rational (AF's isRational\_two), faithful (AF's injective\_twoDimHom), not the character of any representation with matrix entries in Q (QuaternionGroup.not\_exists\_trace\_eq\_twoDimHom: it would be faithful of degree 2, against AF's not\_injective\_rat\_two), while 2 chi is, by left multiplication on the rational quaternions Q\^4 (QuaternionGroup.ratQuaternionHom, trace\_ratQuaternionHom). Blocked by (exact): (1) the lower bound of the Schur-index sentence over Q: if c psi is the character of a representation over Q then m \<= c (indeed m \| c; Isaacs, Character Theory of Finite Groups, Cor. 10.2), so that m is the least number of copies; missing theory: the simple component of Q\[G\] at the Galois orbit of chi as M\_r(D), D a division algebra with centre Q(chi) and index m, whose maximal subfields are splitting fields of degree m realising chi (Tau Ceti has central simple algebras, maximal subfields and splitting, TauCeti.Algebra.CentralSimple and BrauerGroup, but nothing linking them to group algebras and characters); (2) the same sentence over k = R, which the LMFDB also tabulates (irrR\_degree, linR\_degree): m\_R(chi) copies of the real orbit sum afforded over R and no fewer; route clear but not done: positivity of FDRep.schurIndex R (realisation over the top intermediate field C), restriction of scalars C -\> R with Tr\_\{C/R\}(z) = z + conj z for the upper bound, and for the lower bound a real representation with character chi realises V (FDRep.nonempty\_iso\_of\_character\_eq; Tau Ceti's frobeniusSchurIndicator\_eq\_one\_iff\_isRealizableOverReal). Judgement call (author): read as a possibility claim ('may be needed', exemplified) plus the role of the Schur index (m copies always suffice, proved), the sentence would be covered, as the AF review's 'or at least the knowl's example completed' allows, and the knowl would be formalised; left partial under the ruling of 2026-11-04 (when in doubt, partial) because 'the Schur index plays a role' most naturally means 'exactly m copies are needed'. Review (AG1): partial, confirmed. Blockers i-iii of round AF are closed as stated there (i: concrete instances checked, Multiplicative (ZMod 2 x ZMod 2) and DihedralGroup 2; iii: k = R as tabulated by the LMFDB); iv is half closed. FDRep.schurIndex is the LMFDB's (group.representation.schur\_index: least \[E : Q(chi)\] over Q(chi) \<= E \<= C realising V), equal to the classical multiplicity form only by the missing lower bound, and the upper bound is a genuine restriction-of-scalars theorem, not true by definition. The Schur-index sentence is read with the knowl's 'For fields R of characteristic 0, these values can be characterized in terms of the character table of G': over k = Q and R that characterisation needs the characters afforded over k to be exactly the N-combinations of the m\_k(chi) psi\_chi, so the sentence states that exactly m copies are needed (the lower bound), over both fields the LMFDB tabulates. Blocked by: the lower bound, that m\_k(chi) divides the multiplicity of chi in every character afforded over k (Isaacs, Cor. 10.2), for k = Q (missing theory: the simple components of Q\[G\] as matrix algebras over division algebras of index m) and for k = R, where the upper bound (m\_R(chi) copies of the real orbit sum afforded over R) is missing too. Whether the upper bound and the example are enough is question 1 of review/AG1\_linear\_groups.md; under either answer the knowl stays partial for now (the real case). Review changes: FDRep.sum\_faithful\_iff restated for any set s of conjugates inside galoisConjugates (realCharacter\_faithful\_iff is then a one-line application, and so would be AF's rationalCharacter\_faithful\_iff); FDRep.exists\_character\_eq\_zero became