# Hypergeometric motives

* [`hgm.degree`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Hypergeometric-motives/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_hgm___degree_FLQQ_--statement) — Degree of a hypergeometric motive. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* hypergeometric motives and their realisations, with dimension sum phi(a) Note: Done: Partial by the sweep of 2026-11-06 (the user's rulings: when in doubt, partial; an unproved fact stated in the knowl makes it partial; a model of the knowl's object is partial): model. The knowl defines the degree of a motive as the dimension of its cohomological realisations and gives Σφ(a\_j) = Σφ(b\_j) as its value for hypergeometric motives; LeanBridge formalises only the formula on the parameters (Parameters.degree, and motiveDegree, the sum of the recipe's Hodge vector), while hypergeometric motives and their realisations are formalised nowhere, as the docstrings say. The formula replaces the knowl's object: combinatorial data for motives, a model (rule 2). Not formalised: “Associated to a motive are vector spaces coming from cohomology of an algebraic variety. The dimension of these vector spaces is the \*\*degree\*\* of the motive.”.
