* [`mf.bianchi.base_change`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Bianchi-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_mf___bianchi___base_change_FLQQ_--statement) — Base-change Bianchi modular forms. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* existence of base change (Langlands) and the cuspidality claims; a proof of the eigenvalue normalisation Note: Done: Moved to partial on 2026-11-01 (user ruling: a formalisation that assumes something is partial). Base change as a relation between a classical newform f of weight w and a Hecke eigenform of weight 2w-2 (LMFDB convention F : H3 -\> C\^\{2w-1\}) over an imaginary quadratic K of any class number on the round of 31 October's class-group tuples of Bianchi modular forms, cuspidal or not (so the Eisenstein base change of a CM-by-K form is covered), with a\_P = a\_p (split/ramified) and a\_p\^2 - 2chi(p)p\^\{w-1\} (inert) at every P \| p, p not dividing N, P not dividing the level, nonprincipal P included; also for the round of 31 October's newforms of every weight (class number 1), equal to the round of 29 October's relation in weight 2. Proved: the eigenvalues agree at the primes over the same p (Aut(K)-invariance); the knowl's case split is the residue degree, so the relation says a\_P = alpha\_p\^r + beta\_p\^r, the T-coefficient of L\_p\^\{(r)\}(f,T); and, with the central character chi o N of the base change, the Euler factors then satisfy the round of 29 October's IsBaseChangeOfEulerFactors over Q, so this base change is the special case of mf.base\_change the knowl mentions ('is a base change' is IsBaseChangeFromRat). Not proved: existence (Langlands) and the knowl's cuspidality claims; deviations: the knowl's formula assumes a trivial nebentypus (chi(p) is kept), base changes with ramified central character chi o N are not Gamma\_0(N)\_b-forms, and the eigenvalue normalisation N(P)\^\{(w-2)/2\} T\_P is the round of 31 October's (hand-checked by its reviewer; with k = 2w-2 it turns the unitary eigen