* [`mf.bianchi.spaces`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Bianchi-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_mf___bianchi___spaces_FLQQ_--statement) — Spaces of Bianchi modular forms. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* the rational and integral structures (the cohomology of Γ₀(𝔑), Eichler–Shimura–Harder, absent from the pins); finite dimension and Hecke stability for congruence subgroups other than Γ₀(𝔑) and for weight 0 Note: Done: Proved at level Gamma\_0(N), N != 0, k \>= 1, K imaginary quadratic of class number 1: M\_k(N) and S\_k(N) are finite dimensional (reduction theory by Minkowski, a Sturm bound, and two values of the constant term at finitely many cusps); the Petersson inner product, Hermitian and definite, and new = old\^perp (mem\_bianchiNewSubspace\_iff); T\_p self-adjoint for p not dividing N and the adjoint of U\_q is W\_N U\_q W\_N; all T\_p commuting and preserving old and new; S\_k = old + new, direct; and, for the newforms: they span the newspace (span\_range\_toFun), the distinct ones are pairwise orthogonal (bianchiPetersson\_toFun\_eq\_zero) and linearly independent (linearIndependent\_range\_toFun), and every simultaneous eigenform of the T\_p, p not dividing N, in the newspace is an eigenform of all T\_q (exists\_bianchiHeckeTPrimeCusp\_eq\_smul). Unproved: the rational and integral structures (cohomology, absent from the pins), and finite dimension and Hecke stability for congruence subgroups other than Gamma\_0(N) and for k = 0. The knowl's 'a Galois extension of Q of degree d' and 'the Hecke operators are all self-adjoint' fail in general (both recorded).
