* [`cmf.fricke`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Classical-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_cmf___fricke_FLQQ_--statement) — Fricke involution. Difficulty: hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The involution w\_N of the modular curve X₀(N) over ℚ (ag.modcurve.x0; round AF has it on the Riemann surface Γ₀(N)\\ℍ\*) and the identification of the action it induces on S\_k(Γ₀(N)) with the Fricke operator. Declarations (Tau Ceti): `TauCeti.normalizedFrickeOperatorCusp`, `TauCeti.Nat.IsExactDivisor.normalizedAtkinLehnerOperatorCusp`, `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.frickeSign`. Note: Done: Round AF (AF2). Closed: the sign and the parity. The L-function attached to a newform f in S\_k\^new(Gamma\_0(N)) is now an AnalyticLFunction (see lfunction.conductor) whose sign is rootNumber = i\^k lambda\_N(f) (sign\_analyticLFunction); for trivial nebentypus the weight is even (Tau Ceti's parity lemma) and lambda\_N(f) is the Fricke eigenvalue, so the sign is i\^\{-k\} times the eigenvalue of w\_N (rootNumber\_eq\_I\_zpow\_neg\_mul\_frickeSign). As f is self-dual, the sign is (-1)\^r with r the analytic rank (IsSelfDual.rootNumber\_eq\_neg\_one\_pow\_analyticRank), so in weight 2, where i\^\{-2\} = -1, the analytic rank is even exactly when w\_N f = -f (even\_analyticRank\_iff\_frickeSign\_eq\_neg\_one), and odd exactly when w\_N f = +f (odd\_analyticRank\_iff\_frickeSign\_eq\_one, added by the AF2 review: the author left it as a composite with frickeSign\_eq\_one\_or\_neg\_one; it replaces IsSelfDual.rootNumber\_eq\_neg\_one\_pow\_analyticRank in the links, which stays linked under cmf.analytic\_rank). Remaining gap, unchanged: '(induced by the corresponding involution on the modular curve X\_0(N))' needs the involution w\_N of X\_0(N) and the action it induces on S\_k(Gamma\_0(N)); X\_0(N) is partial (ag.modcurve.x0: no algebraic curve, and the compact Riemann surface Gamma\_0(N)\\H\* of CompactRiemannSurface.lean has no w\_N), so this is the same gap as cmf.atkin-lehner's last sentence. Previous category: Partially in Tau Ceti; the new links are LeanBridge's. 'omega\_N' for w\_N is a pure typo. No weight-2 newform is constructed in the trees; the general-weight statements apply to deltaNewform. AF2 review: the parenthetical is a claim, not an explanatory remark (ruling of 2026-11-06: an unproved fact the text states, remarks included, keeps a knowl partial; it is not a 'special case of' cross-reference): it says that the operator w\_N on S\_k(Gamma\_0(N)) is induced by the involution of X\_0(N), i.e. that f(z) (dz)\^\{k/2\} pulls back to (f \|\_k W\_N)(z) (dz)\^\{k/2\} under z -\> -1/(Nz) with the normalised W\_N. AF3's ModularCurve/AtkinLehner.lean builds the involution of Gamma\_0(N)\\H\* (atkinLehnerX0), not its action on forms. Blocked by: the involution w\_N of the modular curve X\_0(N) (ag.modcurve.x0; AF3 has it on the Riemann surface Gamma\_0(N)\\H\*) and the identification of the action it induces on S\_k(Gamma\_0(N)) (holomorphic differentials for k = 2) with the Fricke operator. Not formalised: “(induced by the corresponding involution on the modular curve \$X\_0(N)\$)”.
