* [`mf`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Modular-forms-miscellaneous/#--informal-preview-mf--statement) — Modular form (general). Difficulty: medium, information. *Blocked by:* a precise notion of modular form of a given weight and multiplier system in the knowl (per kind), and the vector-space statement for each (Maass forms only with a fixed eigenvalue) Declarations (Mathlib): `ModularForm`. Note: Done: Partial by the sweep of 2026-11-06 (the user's rulings: when in doubt, partial; an unproved fact stated in the knowl makes it partial; a model of the knowl's object is partial): reading. The umbrella text covers classical, Maass, Hilbert, Bianchi and Siegel forms with weights and multiplier systems and asserts the vector-space property for all of them; ModularForm.multiplierSpace is only the elliptic, holomorphic, integral-weight case (k : ℤ, v : Γ →\* Circle, so no half-integral weight multiplier systems), where it holds by construction. For Maass waveforms the statement as written fails (a sum of eigenfunctions with different Laplace eigenvalues is not one), so the knowl needs a precise reading per kind. Not formalised: “The term \*\*modular form\*\* is used to describe several types of complex functions which have a certain type of functional equation and growth condition. ... Modular forms of the same weight and multiplier system that are defined over the same group form a \$\\mathbb\{C\}\$-vector space.”.
* [`mf.base_change`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Modular-forms-miscellaneous/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_mf___base_change_FLQQ_--statement) — Base change of a GL(2) modular form. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* the knowl's last sentence at every prime rather than almost all (strong multiplicity one for GL(2) over K, and the Hecke eigenvalues at the bad primes, which the framework does not define); secondary: no cuspidal base change over K ≠ ℚ (existence of base change, or the Hilbert and Bianchi comparison maps); a judgement call for the user, since every notion the knowl defines is captured Note: Done: The adelic lift of a classical cusp form of level Gamma1(N) is built and proved to be a cuspidal automorphic form on GL2(A\_Q) (master formula, smoothness, K\_inf-finiteness, Casimir eigenvalue k(k-2)/2, central character the Hecke character of the nebentypus, boundedness, cuspidality for the framework's constant term); for a newform it is a Hecke eigenform with a\_v = p\^(1-k/2) a\_p and arithmetic Euler factor 1 - a\_p T + chi(p) p\^(k-1) T\^2 (review: matches LMFDB 1.12.a.a at p = 2, 3 with Tau Ceti's tau(2), tau(3)), so Delta gives a concrete nonzero cuspidal Hecke eigenform, and g over K is a base change of the lift of f exactly when its Euler factors are 1 - s\_r T + (chi(p) p\^(k-1))\^r T\^2 at almost all primes. Still missing: the knowl's last sentence at every prime (proved only at almost all primes: needs strong multiplicity one for GL(2) over K and eigenvalues at the bad primes), and any cuspidal base change over a field K other than Q (no comparison maps with Hilbert or Bianchi forms, no existence of base change).
* [`mf.cm`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Modular-forms-miscellaneous/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_mf___cm_FLQQ_--statement) — Complex multiplication. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* strong multiplicity one over F, for the converse of 'or equivalently' and for 'χ quadratic' from the eigenvalues when F ≠ ℚ; and a Hecke eigenform with CM (no CM newform at the pins) Note: Done: HasCMBy now also asks the form to be nonzero (edit of the committed ComplexMultiplication.lean and SelfTwistHecke.lean), so HasCM 0 no longer holds. For the adelic lift of a classical newform f and a primitive nontrivial Dirichlet character psi, the knowl's condition a\_p = psi(p) a\_p at the good primes holds exactly when f has a self twist by psi (cmf.self\_twist), psi is then quadratic (review: isQuadratic\_of\_hasCMEigenvalues\_adelicLift, so over Q 'chi is quadratic' follows from the eigenvalues alone), and complex multiplication of the lift in the representation sense gives the classical self twist. Still missing: a concrete Hecke eigenform with CM (none at the pins: only Delta, which has no CM), and over a general F the converse of 'or equivalently' and 'chi is quadratic' from the eigenvalues alone, which need strong multiplicity one for GL(2) over F. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/ModularForms/README.md:996
